k><name>MITSUI CHEMICALS, INCORPORATED</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGAWA, SHINJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUKEGAWA, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUKAWA SUSUMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IRIZATO YOSHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATOH TOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MACHIDA KATSUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OGAWA SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUKEGAWA MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKAWA, SUSUMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IRIZATO, YOSHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATOH, TOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MACHIDA, KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGAWA, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUKEGAWA, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for producing a polysuccinimide having a weight-average molecular weight of 40,000 or higher, which comprises: the step (1) of mixing and heating aspartic acid and an acid catalyst to produce a liquid low-molecular polymer mixture; the step (2) of moderately separating the acid catalyst from the liquid mixture to directly change the polymer-containing liquid phase to a solid phase and thereby produce a solid low-molecular polymer mixture; and the step (3) of subjecting the resultant solid mixture to solid state polymerization. The process can be conducted with a simple apparatus and is free from problems such as generation of a highly viscous phase, excessive foaming, and reaction product bulking.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Procédé servant à préparer un polysuccinimide dont le poids moléculaire moyen en poids est égal ou supérieur à 40.000, ce qui consiste à :(1) mélanger et à réchauffer de l'acide aspartique et un catalyseur acide afin d'obtenir un mélange polymère liquide de poids moléculaire bas ; (2) séparer avec modération le catalyseur acide du mélange liquide, de façon à modifier directement la phase liquide contenant le polymère en une phase solide et, de ce fait, obtenir un mélange solide polymère de poids moléculaire bas ; (3) soumettre le mélange solide obtenu à une polymérisation à l'état solide. On peut exécuter ce procédé au moyen d'un dispositif simple, ce qui élimine des problèmes tels que la génération d'une phase extrêmement visqueuse, la production excessive de mousse et le gonflement du produit réactionnel.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/lega